<<<
We are utterly, hopelessly, irretrievably, ruined; It is theoretically certain, but practically doubtful; He may probably or possibly be in time. These are all irteproachable; in the first, each of the three adverbs expresses degree about ruined;
===
*We are utterly, hopelessly, irretrievably, ruined; It is theoretically certain, but practically doubtful; He may probably or possibly be in time.* These are all irreproachable; in the first, each of the three adverbs expresses degree about *ruined*;
>>>

<<<
in all cases the -ly adverbs are strictly parallel.
===
in all cases the *-ly* adverbs are strictly parallel.
>>>

